<title>POLAND: Polish grain prices fall at last week's auctions.</title>
<headline>Polish grain prices fall at last week's auctions.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish Agriculture Ministry said in a statement that average prices of wheat, rye and barley all fell at last week's grain auctions.</p>
<p>POLISH FARM AUCTION PRICES (AVERAGE)</p>
<p>  Product   week to Oct 26    previous week    yr/yr change</p>
<p>   Wheat	64.01 zl/q	 65.33 zl/q	  64.1 pct</p>
<p>   Rye	  43.29 zl/q	 43.39 zl/q	  65.4 pct</p>
<p>   Barley     53.68 zl/q	 54.45 zl/q	  54.3 pct</p>
<p>NOTE: zl/q = zlotys per quintal.</p>
<p>--Warsaw Newsroom+48 22 653 9700</p>
